ions would go away for some period  of time this is a tax break people would  get more money on their paychecks what's  wrong with that so the problem with a  payroll tax cut  is how you're going to design it but  also what it's supposed to achieve so  one of the reasons why there could be an  economic problem right now it's not so  much because people don't want to spend  money or don't have enough cash but it's  because they actually are trying to  limit their commercial activities they  try to not go to the theater they're  trying to not go to the restaurant  they're basically they're not  cash-strapped they just basically  forcing some savings on themselves  because of the health issue so if you do  a payroll tax cut that is on the  employee side you're just really very  likely not going to be increasing the  incentive for people to interact more in  places where the virus they could catch  the virus on the employer side I mean  it's it's questionable I mean it is true  that a lot of small businesses that are  faced with a decrease in demand for  their products it may benefit from from  it but can the reduction be big enough  and fast enough to compensate for all  this loss in demand it's just hard to  see if this continues for a long time I  mean the kind of payroll tax really if  you would need is not something that  this government can afford right so it's  hard to make a case for fiscal stimulus  when goods aren't being produced and  people aren't leaving their homes to go  buy more stuff yeah exactly and but  again it's really important to  understand that the way fiscal stimulus  usually works is by changing people's  behavior and it's hard to see when the  reason why people aren't consuming  things is because they don't want to go  to stores they don't want to be because  they don't want to go to restaurants  because they don't want to be infected  they don't want to go to the movies  because they don't want to be infected  how giving them more money is g